red across if/else arms (`if(C){print "x"}else{print "x"}` hash-conses to ONE Str Constant) had its GEP emitted branch-locally in the first arm, so the sibling arm's use was not dominated (lli "Instruction does not dominate all uses"). FIX (Chalk-only): the Str-const GEP is a pure pointer to a module global -> emit it in the ENTRY block (dominates every block), the same rule the Int/Boolean constant cases already use. Corpus D1e (`if($x==1){print "same"}else{print "same"} 1`). elsif.t now PASSES whole-file (three PASSes: if.t, cond.t, elsif.t). floor 145->146. Prior: positional `$_[N]` argument binding + call-result repr propagation (t/cmd/elsif.t drain, partial). THREE Chalk-only fixes: (1) _collect_positional_arg_reads recognizes a `$_[0]` Subscript (container Constant("_"), index Constant(0)) as a positional arg read, bound to the caller's arg like a `shift @_` (keyed by refaddr, consulted before _lower_subscript); single positional only, multiple `$_[N]` / mixed shift+subscript GAP. (2) _seed_direct_call_arg_reprs stamps a `$_[0]` read from the caller's arg repr (monomorphic, like the shift path) so the callee body types. (3) the call-stamping passes (_resolve_direct_calls + _seed_direct_call_arg_reprs) now iterate _all_graph_nodes (nodes + control-chain) so a Call embedded in an if CONDITION (`if (($x = foo(1)) == 1)`) -- absent from $g->nodes -- gets its result repr stamped, and a final _seed_and_propagate_reprs pass flows the now-typed Call into its `$x = foo()` Assign consumer. Corpus F8 (`sub f { $_[0] + 1 } f(10)` -> 11). elsif.t's NEXT blocker is a shared string-constant GEP that does not dominate all its branch uses (lli "Instruction does not dominate all uses"). floor 144->145. Prior: MULTI-EXIT VALUE MERGE lands: a mid-body `last if D` in a CONDITIONAL loop `while(C){ STMT; last if D } $x` where a slot rebound before the break is READ POST-LOOP. The loop exits via TWO paths -- header-false (C fails) OR the break (D true) -- which disagree on the slot value, needing a real exit Phi. The producer already builds it [header-Phi, break-value]; the backend GAPped ("loop-exit Region has N LIVE Phi consumer(s)"). FIX (Chalk-only): record each mid-body-last break arm's block label (_record_break_block into the loop ctx), then in the exit block emit `phi [header-Phi-value, %header], [break-point-value, %break-block]` per LIVE exit Phi (header input first, break inputs aligned to the exit Region's predecessor order). Both exit-value refs (the header Phi and the loop-body Add) are computed in the header block, which dominates the exit. Corpus T4d (`while($x<100){$x=$x+1; last if $x==3} $x` -> 3, break path; bilateral: break-not-taken exits header-false, also 3). The HEADLESS while(1) mid-body last (T4c) stays a GAP -- it needs headless-loop body discovery, separate. floor 143->144. Prior: SECOND WHOLE-FILE t/base PASS: t/base/cond.t lowers end-to-end (lli==perl, via Mode1Runner). Its last blocker was `==`/`!=` NUMERIC comparison of Str operands (`$x == $x` where $x is a string): _lower_icmp_int emitted `icmp i64` on the raw i8* ptrs. FIX (Chalk-only): when either operand is Num or Str, perl numifies both -> coerce each to a double (Int via sitofp, Str via @chalk_str_to_num leading-numeric, Num passthrough) and `fcmp` (ordered o* for </<=/>/>=/==, unordered une for !=). Both-Int keeps the i64 fast path unchanged. Corpus L9 (`"0"=="0"` -> 1), L9b (`" 3"=="3"` byte-unequal but numerically equal -> 1, proves numify not memcmp), L9c (`"0"!="1"` -> 1). floor 140->143. Prior: last-statement `&&`/`||` with a Boolean guard + a print arm now lowers -- the t/base/cond.t idiom `$x eq $x && (print ...)` / `$x ne $x || (print ...)` as the LAST statement (OPf_WANT=0, its value is the block return, NOT OPf_WANT_VOID). Unlike L5 (mid-body, trailing 1 -> control flow), the last-statement form is a value-returning And/Or over BOTH Boolean operands (a StrEq guard and a print's builtin::is_bool return). The backend rejected the Boolean LHS (only